Pre-diff review criteria (written before inspecting implementation diff)

1. Structured lifetime: scope exit joins every child and cleanup, releases owned channels/shares/records. Child failure cancels siblings and body, selects least actual failing path, reaches scope caller once.
2. Cooperative cancellation: each scheduler suspension checks applicable cancellation, never interrupts pure code; unstarted tasks drop. Started tasks unwind inner delimiter exactly once, innermost final first, preserving services and an active outer scheduling boundary. Cleanup is shielded from older cancellation; fresh cleanup scopes still handle their own failures.
3. Race records first observed completion, cancels loser and waits cleanup; previously observed failure wins. Outcome and cleanup completion are separate; shielded join on accepted cancelled outcome stops immediately.
4. FIFO ready queue and channel partner order; source-order choice; one transaction per sync, no self rendezvous, losers withdrawn before wake; mappers only after commit in winner task. Cancellation removes all registrations. Check-and-sleep cannot lose wakeups.
5. Quiescence: only no runnable/pending delivery AND no program-root outstanding or explicitly borrowed producer work is deadlock. Unrelated/control roots and observer cells alone do not count. Poll only for actual blocked request interest; nested routes preserve this.
6. Request identity/state/one-shot take: Ready survives group close; cancel-all touches outstanding only; close forbids future starts; borrowed await does not own producer, owned await cancels on unwind; observers unsubscribe; table slots/generations cannot alias reused work; normal/stop teardown drops host work.
7. Deterministic pure FIFO and scripted runs across O0/O2 and Rust/JS; paths share spawn/run counter; random uses full supplied generator and semantic path, not schedule. Real IO completion order is explicitly not deterministic.
8. Types: API schemes and child errors/services match runtime sections 5/6. Escaped Task is allowed as a value, join outside scope must stop; nonportable capture is allowed/pinned, portable sends/results/shares must stop. Missing ordinary child service must remain in inferred entry requirements. Invariant handles and covariant Events/Requests.
9. Complexity: amortized constant ready queue, channel-local waiters, per-scope live counters; assess full switch cost separately. Repeat reported primitive benchmarks and distinguish scheduler data objects from compiler capture/frame/boxed allocations.

References read before diff: Go proc.go checkdead/runqput, chan.go enqueue/dequeue, select.go registration/loser dequeue; Eio switch.ml fail/await_idle/run_internal and cancel.ml protect/cancel_internal; Trio _run.py Nursery child_finished/nested_child_finished and cancellation shield rules; GHC RaiseAsync.c blocked MVar revocation and masked handler entry; CML event.sml atomic transaction/cleanup, channel.sml queues and transaction ids. References are source-read, not yet executed. Differences allowed by spec: Go has no automatic structured scope, Go select randomizes alternatives; Trio/Eio aggregate exceptions rather than least-path error; i cleanup shielding is automatic on cancellation and non-yielding code may monopolize single worker.
